      "status": "approve",
      "reviewer": "/root/research_b",
      "reasoning": "Primary MediaDBcompound38 and both complete TAP snapshots support an ionic Zn2+ nutrient representation. They do not establish metallic zinc or an experimentally supplied zinc salt. I additionally read Boyle2009: it references TAP via Harris1989 without giving a zinc reagent in the article. The revised decision retains the legitimate ion concept but withdraws the actionable owner proposal pending supplied-material context; it does not call the ion identifier itself wrong.",
